n provided. All interested parties are responsible for their own independent enquiries in order to determine whether or not this information is in fact accurate.','townhouse','Ropes Crossing',-33.72801462,150.78449568,2760,'NSW','10/30 Australis Drive','Ropes Crossing',2,4,2,'Laing+Simmons - The Abassi Group','Garage: 1, Open Spaces: 1, Secure Parking, Air Conditioning, Built-in Wardrobes, Dishwasher, Ensuite: 1, Floorboards'),(795,'BEAUTIFUL APARTMENT IN BOX HILL',550,'As good as it gets...two bedrooms, ground floor with small backyard and solid brick unit. Light, bright and yours to occupy.<br/><br/>Offering master bedroom, both with built in robes, main bathroom that has bathtub and shower and internal laundry. Good size separate living room area leads out to the small back yard, where you can sit and entertain. Renovated kitchen with electric appliances.<br/><br/>Additional features include: <br/>- single carport<br/><br/>Most important is the close proximity to Box Hill Railway Station and Melbourne\'s second largest Bus Depot, Centro Shopping Centre and Wet Market and Carrington Rd and Station Street Restaurants.','apartment','Box Hill',-37.82458400,145.11932600,3128,'Vic','3/35 Kent Road','Box Hill',1,2,1,'RT Edgar','Carport: 1'),(796,'Vintage Charm in West Launceston’s Heart',580,'Nestled in the heart of West Launceston, this delightful 1920s home blends character charm with modern comfort. Thoughtfully presented and welcoming, the property showcases high ceilings, polished timber floors and classic architectural details creating a light filled, timeless living experience. With three spacious bedrooms, versatile living spaces and a generous outdoor area, this home offers both immediate comfort and future potential. Positioned just moments from local cafes, parks, schools and the iconic Cataract Gorge, it’s a rare opportunity to secure a residence that truly captures the spirit and convenience of West Launnie living.<br/><br/>TERMS OF TENANCY:<br/>Rent: $580 per week<br/>Available: 9th March 2026<br/>Lease Length: 12 month lease preferred<br/>Pet Policy: Pets are considered upon application<br/>Inspection: Please register for inspections online<br/>Apply: Online – Realestate.com.au<br/><br/>HOW TO APPLY:<br/>Submit your application via the \"APPLY\" button on Realestate.com.au<br/><br/>PROPERTY FEATURES:<br/>- Charming character home with original 9 foot ceilings and period features <br/>- Polished timber floorboards throughout with carpeted bedrooms<br/>- Open plan lounge and dining areas, filled with plenty of natural light <br/>- Good sized kitchen with garden outlook and large walk in pantry <br/>- Three well appointed bedrooms, two with original decorative fireplaces <br/>- Family bathroom with a gorgeous claw-foot bath <br/>- Large laundry with potential to double as a mudroom <br/>- Dishwasher included<br/>- Reverse cycle heating for year round comforts <br/>- Fully fenced, low maintenance backyard<br/>- Single garage with secure parking for one vehicle <br/>- Outdoor entertaining area ready for gatherings and barbecues <br/><br/>ABOUT THE AREA:<br/>West Launceston is one of the city’s most tightly held and highly regarded suburbs, loved for its leafy streets, classic homes and strong community feel. Sitting just minutes from the Launceston CBD, it offers the perfect balance of inner-city convenience and relaxed residential living. The area is particularly prized for its elevation, quiet surrounds and beautiful character homes that reflect the suburb’s rich history.<br/><br/>Residents enjoy easy access to everyday essentials alongside some of Launceston’s best lifestyle offerings, including local cafés, schools, parks and walking tracks. The iconic Cataract Gorge Reserve is close by, providing a spectacular natural playground right on the city’s edge, while public transport and major road links make commuting effortless. West Launceston continues to attract professionals, families and downsizes alike, thanks to its charm, livability and enduring appeal.','house','West Launceston',-41.44979564,147.13193306,7250,'Tas','12 Esther Street','West Launceston',1,3,1,'Harrison Agents - Launceston','Courtyard, Fully Fenced, Garage: 1, Outdoor Entertaining Area, Secure Parking, Air Conditioning, Broadband Internet Available, Dishwasher, Floorboards'),(797,'A Home That Simply Works - Comfort, Freshness, and Easy Living',495,'Set behind a quiet street presence, 299 Balston Street, Lavington offers a thoughtfully refreshed home designed for renters who value comfort, functionality, and a space that feels genuinely easy to live in.<br/><br/>From the moment you step inside, the home presents clean lines, fresh finishes, and a sense of calm continuity throughout. Newly painted interiors and brand-new carpets create a crisp, welcoming atmosphere, a blank canvas ready to adapt to your lifestyle without feeling sterile or impersonal.<br/><br/>The open-plan kitchen, living, and dining area forms the heart of the home. Designed for everyday living rather than show, this space allows for natural flow between cooking, relaxing, and entertaining. A gas cooktop anchors the kitchen, offering reliability and efficiency, while the reverse-cycle split system ensures year-round comfort, warm in winter, cool in summer, and effortless to manage.<br/><br/>All three bedrooms are well-proportioned and fitted with ceiling fans, providing additional climate comfort and quiet circulation. One bedroom includes a built-in robe, ideal for streamlined storage, while the remaining rooms offer flexibility, perfect for a home office, guest room, or personal retreat.<br/><br/>The fully refurbished bathroom brings a modern touch to daily routines, with updated finishes that feel fresh, clean, and practical. A separate laundry adds further convenience, keeping household tasks neatly out of sight and well-organised.<br/><br/>Outside, the enclosed yard provides a secure, low-maintenance space suitable for relaxed outdoor use, whether that\'s a morning coffee, a small garden project, or simply a private area to unwind. Two garden sheds offer valuable additional storage, keeping the yard functional without clutter. A single carport completes the package, providing sheltered off-street parking.<br/><br/>Apply Here! https://snug.com/apply/raywhitealbury','house','Lavington',-36.05252178,146.95015250,2641,'NSW','299 Balston Street','Lavington',1,3,1,'Ray White - Albury North','Carport: 1'),(798,'Beautifully Presented Family Home in the Heart of Longueville',1500,'Perched on the high side of the road with pretty outlook and water glimpses, this quality home is a few minutes to the ferry wharf and bus access to prestige schools nearby.<br/><br/>- Four good size bedrooms, master with walk in robe and en suite<br/>- Featuring a beautiful timber deck, completely private and tranquil<br/>- Modern white kitchen with quality appliances<br/>- A choice of formal and casual living and dining areas<br/>- Plenty of natural light, under floor heating, timber floors<br/>- High ceilings, lush gardens, parking for 2 cars plus a single garage<br/>- Lovely tiered gardens, elevated sunny position<br/>- Premier schools, local shops and cafes nearby<br/><br/><br/>**To register for an inspection, submit an enquiry at the bottom of the page to receive the registration link.**<br/><br/>**ADVERTISED INSPECTION TIMES displayed on this page are subject to cancellation or change, please favourite the property in order to receive updates on property inspection and property detail changes**','house','Longueville',-33.82764156,151.16722663,2066,'NSW','38 Dettmann Avenue','Longueville',3,4,2,'McGrath Lane Cove -','Carport: 2'),(799,'Pet friendly studio with a desk, spacious balcony & full size kitchen | 2 weeks rent free*',680,'Sign a new lease today and enjoy exclusive rent-free offers: <br/>• 2 Weeks Free on 12 Month Lease*<br/>• 4 Weeks Free on 24 Months Lease*<br/>• 1 Week Free on 6 Month Lease*<br/><br/>Book a privat