om continues the modern aesthetic with quality finishes and full-height tiling within the shower.<br/><br/>Finished with a fresh, contemporary feel throughout, this apartment offers comfort, style and convenience in an excellent location.<br/><br/>Features include:<br/>- Good sized bedroom<br/>- Built-in robes<br/>- Spacious balcony with access from the lounge room<br/>- Internal laundry with dryer<br/>- Storage cage<br/>- Reverse cycle heating and cooling<br/>- Lift access<br/>No current EER <br/><br/>This property has a valid exemption and is not required to comply with the minimum ceiling insulation standard.<br/><br/>This property is awaiting an insulation information from the Owners Corporation.<br/><br/>Suburb Snapshot<br/>Greenway was named in honour of Francis Howard Greenway (1777-1837). Francis Greenway was a Colonial architect and arrived in Sydney as a transportee in 1814. He worked as an architectural adviser on public works from 1814-1815 and was later appointed Civil Architect and Assistant Engineer in 1816. Greenway supervised the construction of a number of public buildings. Howard Greenway also adapted designs and methods to suit the Australian climate.<br/><br/>Disclaimer: <br/>Please note that while all care has been taken regarding general information and marketing information compiled for this rental advertisement, LJ HOOKER CANBERRA CITY does not accept responsibility and disclaim all liabilities in regard to any errors or inaccuracies contained herein. We encourage prospective tenants to rely on their own investigation and in-person inspections to ensure this property meets their individual needs and circumstances.<br/><br/>PETS: <br/>Please be aware that at all stages of tenancy this property requires consent to be sought from the lessor for the keeping of any pets at the premises. Consent must be provided before any pets are at the premises.<br/><br/>RENTING BOOK:<br/>https://www.justice.act.gov.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0008/2443472/Renting-Book-May-2024.pdf','apartment','Greenway',-35.41978885,149.07224993,2900,'ACT','227/12 Limburg Way','Greenway',1,1,1,'LJ Hooker - Canberra City','Balcony, Garage: 1, Air Conditioning, Built-in Wardrobes, Dishwasher'),(3586,'Modern, Spacious & Move In Ready',850,'Step into this near-new, beautifully presented home offering generous space for the whole family and effortless modern living.<br/><br/>Designed with comfort and style in mind, this home features neutral décor and all the modern conveniences you could want. Perfectly located just a short distance to the beautiful Seacliff beach, local shops, schools and public transport options.<br/><br/>Some of the many great features include:<br/>> 4 good size bedrooms, all with built in robes, master suite with walk in robe and ensuite<br/>> Open plan living space with floating floor and sliding glass door to the rear courtyard<br/>> The kitchen boasts stunning stone bench tops, ample cabinetry, stainless steel appliances and gas cooking<br/>> The bathrooms with stone bench tops, double basin and a large freestanding bath <br/>> Laundry with storage cupboards and under stairs storage room<br/>> Double remote garage with internal access and to the rear yard<br/>> Low maintenance front and rear yards, both areas with lawn and irrigation system<br/>> Security alarm system<br/><br/>This easy care property is waiting for you. Register for the first open inspection so you don\'t miss out on the chance to enjoy this stunning home.<br/><br/><br/>\"The Tenant will be responsible to pay for Water Supply & Usage\"<br/><br/>Pets are considered upon application. <br/><br/>IMPORTANT INFORMATION:<br/><br/>Our recommendation is that you book in to the first available inspection to best maximise your chances of securing this fantastic property. <br/>To ensure we are able to update you on any last minute changes to an open inspection please include your mobile number when registering your details. <br/>By booking this inspection you have made an appointment to view the property. <br/>If you are unable to keep this appointment please ensure you cancel your booking via the link on the text you received.<br/><br/>We look forward to meeting you soon.<br/>','house','Seacliff Park',-35.03120671,138.52435852,5049,'SA','1F Lamington Avenue','Seacliff Park',2,4,4,'McGrath Real Estate Group - Glenelg | RLA 252 299','Garage: 2, Open Spaces: 2, Remote Garage, Alarm System, Built-in Wardrobes, Dishwasher, Ducted Cooling, Ducted Heating, Living Areas: 1, Pets Allowed'),(3587,'SUNLIT SPACES AND EFFORTLESS LIVING',510,'Positioned for lifestyle and ease, this thoughtfully designed unit offers modern comforts in a compact, low-maintenance setting. From the sleek kitchen to the private paved courtyard, every space has been designed for relaxed everyday living.<br/><br/>Why you’ll want to move in yesterday:<br/><br/>- 2 bedrooms<br/>- Master with built-in robes and ceiling fan<br/>- Large windows throughout flood the space with natural light.<br/>- Open plan lounge/dining area with ceiling fan <br/>- Contemporary kitchen featuring sleek stainless steel appliances and efficient electric cooking facilities<br/>- Beautiful bathroom with internal laundry space<br/>- Linen cupboard for additional storage<br/>- The kitchen opens onto a private rear yard featuring a paved seating area and a small grassy patch, making it easy to maintain.<br/>- RC/AC in living area directed into the bedrooms to ensure temperature control throughout<br/><br/>Located in sought-after Morphettville, you’ll enjoy easy access to Glenelg Beach, local cafés, quality schools and public transport. With the tram and major road links nearby, commuting to the city is simple while still enjoying a relaxed lifestyle.<br/><br/>The Essentials <br/><br/>Available Date | 6th March<br/>Bond | $2040 <br/>Pets | Negotiable<br/>Lease Term | 12 months<br/>Water Charges | Tenant to pay water usage and water supply<br/>Furnishing | Unfurnished<br/><br/>How It All Works <br/><br/>Please send an enquiry to be notified of open times, it is crucial to register for opens so we can update you if anything changes. Also, enquiry replies often land in junk or spam folders, so keep an eye there if you’re waiting to hear back. We don’twant you to miss out because of tech hiccups. <br/><br/>We’ve done our best to ensure the info here is accurate. Still, it’s always smart to double-check anything important to you. <br/><br/>You’re welcome to get your application ready on Tenant Options in advance. Just a heads-up, we won’t begin processing it until the home has been viewed, either in person or via the virtual tour. If you\'re applying based on the virtual tour, make sure to mention that in your application.','house','Morphettville',-34.98468053,138.54256578,5043,'SA','12/33 Austral Terrace','Morphettville',1,2,1,'Taylored Property','Carport: 1, Fully Fenced, Outdoor Entertaining Area, Built-in Wardrobes, Floorboards, Pets Allowed'),(3588,'Modern 3-Bedroom Townhouse in Prime Mawson Lakes Location!',700,'To apply, please visit www.2apply.com.au. Shortlisted applicants will be also invited to a private inspection.<br/>Please submit an enquiry to register your details and be notified of all available inspection times plus receive our online application form.<br/><br/>Available: 18/03/2026<br/>Long Term Lease<br/>Furniture: Unfurnished or Furnished<br/>SA Water usage and supply charges liable by tenant.<br/><br/>This townhouse is filled with natural light and offers a bright, welcoming home with plenty of space to relax and entertain. Located next to The Cascade Lake, it combines comfort, style, and convenience.<br/><br/>Step inside to discover the open-plan living area, a modern kitchen with walk-in pantry, formal lounge, and a convenient downstairs toilet. Sliding doors open to a covered outdoor entertaining area-perfect for family gatherings or weekend BBQs.<br/><br/>Upstairs, enjoy fresh carpet underfoot, natural light streaming through fixed front windows, and spacious bedrooms.<br/><br/>Key Features:<br/>Master bedroom with ensuite and private balcony<br/>Bedrooms 2 & 3 with built-in robes<br/>Main bathroom with bathtub + third downstairs toilet<br/>Gas stovetop and tiled kitchen/dining area<br/>Ducted reverse-cycle air conditioning for year-round comfort<br/>Large front porch and private rear courtyard<br/>Double lock-up carport with secure roller door <br/><br/>Enjoy the convenience of public transport at your doorstep, or stroll to Mawson Lakes Village for cafes, restaurants, and local shopping. This home truly combines comfort, style, and lifestyle!','house','Mawson Lakes',-34.80139637,138.61042767,5095,'SA','1/83 Augustine Street','Mawson Lakes',2,3,2,'Raine & Horne Unley - RLA301358','Garage: 2'),(3589,'Living At The Griffin',830,'This is not just any apartment, this is The Griffin! Offering timber flooring to all living areas, under-tile heating to all bathrooms, ducted heating and cooling, externally ducted rangehood, feature glass cabinetry and a luxurious 30mm stone benchtop.<br/><br/>Additional amenities include a Wellness Centre with a 25m indoor lap pool, steam room, sauna, uniquely segregated weights and cardio gyms. The Griffin offers a concierge service, available to be your helping hand when you need it - whether it be newspaper deliveries, grocery deliveries (with cold stores available) mail collection and more.<br/><br/>Features include:<br/>- Under-tile heating to all bathrooms<br/>- Elegant kitchen with stone benchtops, glass overhead cabinets and soft close drawers<br/>- Premium Miele appliances and walk-in pantry<br/>- 2.7metre high ceilings<br/>- Floor to ceiling double glazed windows<br/>- Fully ducted reverse cycle heating and cooling<br/>- Quality engineered timber floors<br/>- Fiber optic broadband<br/>- Video intercom system <br/>- Direct pedestrian and bicycle access to Lake Burley Griffin<br/>- Walking distance to iconic Canberra landmarks<br/>No current EER<br/><br/>The property has a valid exemption and is not required to comply with the minimum ceiling insulation standard.<br/><br/>This property features an embedded network for internet NBN Opticom as well as hot water and electricity, with tenants required to connect to Energy locals.<br/><br/>This property is awaiting an insulation information from the Owners Corporation.<br/><br/>Suburb Snapshot<br/>Located in Campbell are the Australian War Memorial, Royal Military College, Duntroon, the Australian Defence Force Academy, and the CSIRO Corporate Headquarters. Also with addresses in the suburb are the \'Ainslie Village\' accommodation centre for people with special needs and the Campbell Park Offices.<br/><br/>Schools located in the suburb include Campbell High School, Campbell Primary School and Canberra Grammar Northside Infant School.<br/><br/>Disclaimer: <br/>Please note that while all care has been taken regarding general information and marketing information compiled for this rental advertisement, LJ HOOKER CANBERRA CITY does not accept responsibility and disclaim all liabilities in regard to any errors or inaccuracies contained herein. We encourage prospective tenants to rely on their own investigation and in-person inspections to ensure this property meets their individual needs and circumstances.<br/><br/>PETS: <br/>Please be aware that at all stages of tenancy this property requires consent to be sought from the lessor for the keeping of any pets at the premises. Consent must be provided before any pets are at the premises.<br/><br/>RENTING BOOK:<br/>https://www.justice.act.gov.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0008/2443472/Renting-Book-May-2024.pdf','apartment','Parkes',-35.28788097,149.13807240,2600,'ACT','163/44 Constitution Avenue','Parkes',2,2,2,'LJ Hooker - Canberra City','Balcony, Garage: 2, Air Conditioning, Built-in Wardrobes, Dishwasher, Ducted Cooling, Ducted Heating, Floorboards, Intercom'),(3590,'Spacious Family Living with Multiple Living Zones!',500,'Available