enities<br/>- Convenient access to main arterial roads for commuting<br/><br/>What to do next:<br/><br/>It is essential that you register for a home open, or to be advised when a viewing time becomes available. Please visit www.hereproperty.com.au and click the \'Book Inspection\' button.<br/><br/>Please ensure you are registered for all viewings so we can keep you updated on any changes.<br/><br/>Once you have viewed the property, you will be sent an SMS and email with a link to apply.','house','Hovea',-31.89724000,116.12714000,6071,'WA','110 Weller Road','Hovea',1,2,4,'HERE Property - LEEDERVILLE','Carport: 4'),(4008,'Refined Family Living in Tralee',820,'PLEASE CLICK \'BOOK INSPECTION\' TO REGISTER & BE NOTIFIED OF UPCOMING INSPECTIONS<br/> <br/>Situated in the growing, family-friendly community of Tralee, this delightful 4-bedroom ensuite home epitomises modern family living. Beautifully finished light-filled family-friendly floorplan has been designed for function & flow with a seamless connection from indoors to out.<br/><br/>The heart of the home is the open plan family/kitchen offering a large, stone-topped island with generous breakfast bar for casual dining. The crisp light kitchen is complemented by a subway-tiled splashback and industrial-inspired pendant lighting elevating the space. Superbly equipped with a large walk-in pantry with exceptional storage, a dishwasher for quick cleanups and a high end induction cooktop, this is a kitchen to inspire the home chef. Sliding door access from the family room to the covered alfresco offers easy indoor/ outdoor flow for easy alfresco dining and entertaining. The main lounge space at the front of the house offers a second living space for the family to gather or use as a home theatre space.<br/><br/>The stunning main bedroom is truly a parent\'s retreat, with a luxurious walk-in robe with custom bespoke storage behind a feature wall and beautiful Australian-made pendant bedside lighting. The elegant adjoining ensuite showcases stone-inspired tiling, a wall-hung vanity topped with a vessel sink for spa-like vibes. The further 3 bedrooms all have built-in robes, plush carpet underfoot and double layer blockout curtains. The family bathroom offers a deep bath for long soaks, a separate shower and the convenience of a separate toilet. Even the spacious laundry with external access has been beautifully finished with generous timber cabinetry, stone-topped benches and subway tiled splashback. Throughout the home, ducted reverse cycle air conditioning provides year-round comfort. The home has an upgraded modern heat pump hot water system, bringing maximum efficiency and energy savings.<br/><br/>The garage offers easy-care epoxy-coated flooring and 15amp power for the home handyman. Along with this there is additional double-gated off-street parking to the rear yard for your caravan, boat & trailer.<br/><br/>Tralee is a suburb on the rise, with sporting facilities, a local school, and thoughtfully designed community spaces, even featuring an outdoor gym, splash park and a huge dog park for the fur members of the family. Framed by the natural beauty of the Tralee Hills and surrounded by expansive open reserves, the area offers a nature-rich lifestyle with room to breathe.<br/><br/>The home is conveniently close to Jerrabomberra, home to two shopping centres, a range of cafés and restaurants, tennis courts, and quality schools. Just moments away lies the vibrant Queanbeyan town centre, Canberra outlet centre in Fyshwick and a short commute to the airport and Majura Park precinct. A few minutes further brings you to Kingston and Manuka, renowned for their boutique shopping, acclaimed dining, cafés, lively pubs and the Public Service precincts around Barton, Capital Hill and Parkes.<br/><br/>Features of the property include;<br/><br/>Contemporary four-bedroom home in the upcoming Tralee community<br/>Formal separate lounge/ home theatre space <br/>Hybrid timber flooring throughout living spaces <br/>Open plan living and dining <br/>Modern kitchen with an induction cooktop, dishwasher, & huge walk in pantry <br/>Over-sized main bedroom with walk in robe and an elegant ensuite <br/>Built-in robes to further 3 bedrooms <br/>Cosy carpets underfoot in all bedrooms <br/>Family bathroom with bath and separate shower <br/>Modern laundry with excellent storage <br/>Ducted reverse cycle air conditioning throughout <br/>Covered rear pergola & easy-care lawn <br/>Double garage with internal access <br/>Additional off-street parking at rear for caravan, boat or trailer<br/>Close to Jerrabomberra & Queanbeyan town centre<br/>Easy access to Fyshwick, Kingston, Manuka and Public Service/Parliamentary working precinct<br/><br/>Available: 27th February 2026<br/><br/>Pets approved on application<br/><br/>HOLDING DEPOSIT<br/>Should your application be successful and you are offered the property a holding deposit will need to be paid within 24 hours, this holding deposit will then form your first 2 weeks rent.<br/><br/>RENT INFORMATION:<br/>1. Rent is collected fortnightly<br/>2. Bond required is equal to 4 weeks rent<br/><br/>DISCLAIMER:<br/>All information regarding this property is from sources we believe to be accurate, however we cannot guarantee its accuracy. Interested persons should make and rely on their own enquiries in relation to inclusions, figures, measurements, dimensions, layout, furniture and descriptions.<br/><br/>RENT INFORMATION:<br/>1. Rent is collected fortnightly unless otherwise nominated for a longer period<br/>2. Bond required is equal to 4 weeks rent<br/><br/>DISCLAIMER:<br/>All information regarding this property is from sources we believe to be accurate, however we cannot guarantee its accuracy. Interested persons should make and rely on their own enquiries in relation to inclusions, figures, measurements, dimensions, layout, furniture and descriptions.','house','Tralee',-35.40330270,149.16506955,2620,'NSW','146 Oxalis Crescent','Tralee'