es room overlooking a large backyard.<br/><br/><br/>The open double drive-through garage provides the benefit of 2 extra car parking spaces, for a boat or caravan. This home offers a practical and harmonious family indoor living layout with a large backyard for outdoor entertainment.<br/><br/><br/>The home comes with many features including 6kw solar panel, evaporative AC and<br/>mature Orange and Pear trees. One garden shed for tenants and one garden shed locked not for use by tenants.<br/><br/>Come to an inspection to see for yourself.<br/><br/><br/>**Please be advised we do not accept online/1Form applications, rental applications can be obtained at viewing. You are not permitted to enter this property unless accompanied by a Heron Johns representative**','house','Willetton',-32.04167000,115.89418000,6155,'WA','4 Werribee Crescent','Willetton',2,4,2,'First National Heron Johns - Bull Creek','Garage: 2, Toilets: 2, Pets Allowed'),(4388,'Partially Furnished in a Convenient Location',500,'Located on Level 1 of the Mezzo complex facing towards Gozzard street, this contemporary partially furnished apartment has got 60 square metres of living and an 8 square metre balcony. Apartment offers open plan kitchen and living dining area.<br/><br/>The kitchen includes stone benches, electric cook top and oven, dishwasher and dryer. Split reverse cycle air conditioning and a European-style laundry with a dryer also included.<br/>The property also has a car space and lift access.<br/><br/>Mezzo complex has got resort style facilities including two landscaped rooftop decks - one featuring a swimming pool, covered alfresco entertaining area, seating and barbecues, pizza oven and a resident\'s library will make you feel like being on a holiday.<br/><br/>Features include:<br/>- Designated study<br/>- Partially furnished <br/>- Smeg kitchen appliances<br/>- Electric cook top and oven<br/>- Dishwasher<br/>- Euro laundry<br/>- Sunny balcony<br/>- Single car space with lift access<br/>- Reverse cycle air conditioning<br/>- NBN ready<br/>- Intercom<br/>- Outdoor entertaining area<br/>*** no storage cage***<br/>No current EER<br/><br/>The property complies with the minimum ceiling insulation standard.<br/><br/>Seeking the section 119 certificate.<br/><br/>There is no embedded Networks for the property. <br/><br/>Suburb Snapshot <br/>The District of Gungahlin is one of the original eighteen districts of the Australian Capital Territory used in land administration. The district is subdivided into divisions (suburbs), sections and blocks. Gungahlin is an Aboriginal word meaning either \"white man\'s house\" or \"little rocky hill\". <br/><br/>The town of Gungahlin was part of the original 1957 plan for future development in the Australian Capital Territory and in 1991 was officially launched as Canberra\'s fourth \'town\' by the Australian Capital Territory Chief Minister. <br/><br/>Within the district is Canberra\'s northernmost town centre that is situated 10 kilometres (6.2 miles) north of Canberra city centre. The town centre is one of five satellites of Canberra, seated in Woden, Tuggeranong, Weston Creek and Belconnen.<br/><br/>Disclaimer: <br/>Please note that while all care has been taken regarding general information and marketing information compiled for this rental advertisement, LJ HOOKER CANBERRA CITY does not accept responsibility and disclaim all liabilities in regard to any errors or inaccuracies contained herein. We encourage prospective tenants to rely on their own investigation and in-person inspections to ensure this property meets their individual needs and circumstances.<br/><br/>PETS: <br/>Please be aware that at all stages of tenancy this property requires consent to be sought from the lessor for the keeping of any pets at the premises. Consent must be provided before any pets are at the premises.<br/><br/>RENTING BOOK:<br/>https://www.justice.act.gov.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0008/2443472/Renting-Book-May-2024.pdf','apartment',