n<br/>Solar hot water system with booster in laundry<br/>5.6KW Solar system (16 solar panels)<br/>Garden shed<br/>Pool storage shed<br/>Mature fruiting Lime and lemon trees<br/>683sqm block<br/><br/><br/>Local Schools<br/>Within walking distance of Calista Primary School (0.8km), St. Vincents Primary School (0.8km), Peter Carnley Anglican Community School (1km), Gilmore College (1.2km), Kings College (2.2km), Murdoch University Rockingham Campus (7km), Kolbe Catholic College (7km)<br/><br/>Travel<br/>Wellard Train Station (1.7km) - Perth and Mandurah train lines<br/>Kwinana Bus station (0.6km) - Local Kwinana suburbs, Rockingham and Fremantle bus routes<br/>Access to Kwinana Freeways North and South via Mortimer Road entry- 3km<br/>Rockingham City Centre 8km, Fremantle 22km, Perth 33km<br/><br/>Beaches<br/>Kwinana Beach (4.1km), Kwinana Dog Beach (5km), Rockingham Foreshore (7.7km)<br/><br/>Local Shopping / Dining<br/>The Kwinana Marketplace (600m) is the central shopping location, which houses major retailers such as Woolworths, Coles and Big W as well as smaller, locally-owned retailers inc medical centres, chemists, clothing outlets, hairdressers, newsagency, takeaway outlets, and petrol stations. This centre is surrounded by other large retailers including Aldi and various service providers, all conveniently located in the heart of Kwinana. These include Dome Kwinana, The Local bar and bistro, Kwinana Recquatic Centre, and Kwinana Public Library to name a few.<br/>The Wellard Village shopping district (1.7km) includes Woolworths, The Well Bar and Bistro, Medical Centre, Bliss Momos cafe, Newsagency, food outlets and other retail stores.<br/><br/>Local Parks<br/>Kwinana has a vast range of parks and ovals ranging in size, purpose and amenities. With sporting ovals and pavilions, the well-known Kwinana Adventure Park (1km), outdoor exercise equipment and accessible parks and playgrounds, there is something for everyone.','house','Parmelia',-32.24858000,115.8184900